# Harbinger of the Tides escaped through Underworld Breach at instant speed owes {2} more (CR 601.2b, 601.2f, 702.138): escape
# lets it be cast from the graveyard but not at instant speed, so in the beginning of combat its own words are what let it be
# cast, with the extra {2}. On turn 1 the Harbinger is cast for {U}{U} (declining the {2}) and Bot1 bolts it. On turn 7 Black
# Lotus pays for Breach, a Lotus Petal is spent, and the Mountains and Mox Ruby are tapped for nothing. In the beginning of
# combat Mox Sapphire and the Island give {U}{U}, the Harbinger's mana cost and the escape's, and the escape is refused for
# the mana ({2}{U}{U} is owed): the Harbinger stays in the graveyard with the three cards it would have exiled. The Lotus
# Petal, an artifact with no flash of any kind, is not offered by escape at all in the beginning of combat.

